{:id :EACL-FORMAL-072
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "custom-codec/numeric-public-cursor-id-reinterpreted-as-native-eid"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before public/native identity domain separation"]
 :affected-backends
 [:shared :datomic :datahike :datalevin :datascript :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "One adapter operation accepted both authenticated public IDs and already-normalized native entity IDs. Its numeric pass-through treated every number as native, so a numeric public cursor or permission-tree identity bypassed the configured public-ID codec."
 :fix
 "Split public identity resolution from native-ID pass-through in the v8 adapter contract; route every public cursor and permission-tree root through the public-only operation; certify the split with a Dafny model, an executed mutation, and a real DataScript multi-page regression."
 :closing-evidence
 ["PublicIdentityBoundary.NumericPublicCursorHasANativeAliasCounterexample"
  "PublicIdentityBoundary.PublicCursorResolutionNeverSelectsNativeIdentity"
  "eacl.formal.executed-mutation-controls/numeric-public-id-native-eid-alias-killed?"
